title: Veeam: Managed server
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a server managed by a Veeam Backup & Replication
 server, collected via the Veeam special agent: a Microsoft Windows or Linux
 server, a VMware vSphere or Cloud Director host, a Hyper-V server or
 cluster, an SCVMM server or an SMB3 server. It reports the server type, its
 availability status, description and roles.

 This check is {OK} if the server is available to Veeam and {CRIT} if it is
 unavailable. Both states are configurable. Any other status, or no status
 at all, is {UNKNOWN}.

 The backup server itself is a managed server too, and is reported with the
 role "Backup server".

 The data can be read with the "Veeam Backup Viewer" role.

discovery:
 One service is created for each managed server reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the managed server.
